Z||000000||Brian Olsovsky||03-03-2000||10:33 PM||||we should talk. sounds like we have the same style engine. is your overbore .060?? i'm stroked to a 3.1. tell me about your injectors. did they make a difference? did you change the fuel reg. and injectors all at once, or one, then the other?? was it worth changing the fuel system? which tank pump did you use?? when i stroked my 2.8 to a 3.1, i wanted the numbers you are getting now but i didn't. we did all the same things, but i'm having problems with fuel delivery. i don't have nitrous yet, but i do need info on superchargers. phone numbers, company names, etc.. please help make my car go faster. i'm not that far away. is fuel my main problem?? does advancing the timing help?? should i put the plenum back on??(just kidding) just tell me what was your most valuable addition to your engine for those 1/4 mile times. are you for real?!?!?!||||reg||4
Z||000001||Brian Olsovsky||03-03-2000||10:47 PM||||i just checked my other topic reply so thanks for the names and info. now that i have your attention, what do you suggest for my engine. i'm estimating about 180-200 h.p. but have never been on a dyno, or on a track.i have an 85 gt with an auto tranny but i installed a shift kit and it seemed to help. i was told that the injectors from a 305 firebird engine would be the same flow rate that i need for my engine, but am not sure. i did the math given from a fuel injection tuning article and it matched up too. what brand pressure regulator did you use and where did you install it on the engine?? was it the factory replacement?? if so, how do you get to the adjustments under the plenum?? lots more questions to ask. i'll keep checking this week.||||reg||5
Z||000002||1FST2M6||03-03-2000||11:01 PM||||you rang....  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>  -my dyno runs, red is nitrous, blue normaly please note these are at the wheels numbers... ad 27.5% for drive line loss.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>  -pics of my car just cause... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net/fiero.htm</A>  -the shop page of my car (oh it can also bee seen at the NOPI show in the NOS Nitrous booth on the "picture pages", under "Ed's notes")... the single most helpful on the Dyno and using my botty-o-meter was the exhaust.. 2.5" Random Cat, 2.5" mandrel piping to 2.5" 2 chamber flowmaster to a single 4" 5Zidgen tip. yes i'm for real Both Raydar and BlackGT (forum members and members of the Georgia Fieros club can vouch for that) I had my injectors cleaned for the normal motor and they were just ok.. then the Nitrous came.. needed LOTS more fuel upgraded to 36#-55#(peak) stock cobra mustang (sn95)injectors that the guys at RC Engineering claibrated and matched for me. The guys at the shop burned me a new chip so my car would run on so much fuel. The intake has been Extrude-honed and the stock exhaust manifolds ported... and wraped with ceramic header tape. the supercharger site I was talking about before (for the EASY bolting is... ) <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A>  -any other questions I'd be more than happy to answer... in addition to the coil have you changed your ignition box (eg. MSD 6al or BTM, or Crane Hi6... if you do get the S?C setup you'll want the MSD 6BTM it will adjust you timing from 0-3* per pound of boost.. free HP) The shop i deal with has quite a list of accomplishment under it's belt... many 500+hp moostangs, even more 500+hp Supra turbos, a 320hp (at the wheels) Mitsubishi Mirage and a host of others they are also the builders and designers of the worlds ONLY Twin Turbo CRX. I'm not really on their list of stupid fast cars it's not really that fast in the grand scheme of 500+hp monsters, but I'm personal friends with them all and the owner lives down the street... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||03-03-2000||11:01 PM||||You probably already know this, but 1FST2M6 is running nitrous to get those fast 1/4mile times.  The 55lb injectors would be way on the extreme side for a non N2O car.  You shouldn't need the big fuel pump either.  The pressure regulator is the small canister like thing under the upper manifold mounted on the drivers side of the fuel rail.  It's black with one vacuum line sticking out of it.  The Fiero store sells them, but you could probably get them cheaper through hypertech who manufactures them.<P>Check out 3.2 0-60 for some reality.  I'm trying to figure out what's keeping this engine down too.  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-03-2000||11:17 PM||||Fuel pump... i think it's from an 88 Iroc 5.7 liter.. the last year of the Iroc got it from napa.. I got it from NAPA. the Holley one from the Fiero store would also do fine 255lph will do great... I chose the first cause I need the pressure the camaro one can run with the nitrous on she'll peak at over 110psi the stock unit would just choke and die when dead headed. the factory fuel pressure unit is being used... altho i did place a nickel under the diaphram (perminate pressure rise) I have a Stillen vacuum assisted fuel pressure riser installed but cant tell a difference in performance at any level on the dyno. I've replace the stock fuel hoses with braided units from Earls (Hydraluic accessories) and the shop worked their magic to make them fit (all they needed was an adapter from Earls, a set of 10an to whatever the stock pitch is) OOOH also when you drop your fuel tank there is a big piece of plastic at the bottom of the pump this unit stops gas from sloshing around and also limits the amount of fuel your pump can injest. pull it out and toss it!  Keep the little filter on it though but toss this piece.  more to follow as I remember it.... Your clutch ok? I'm running an ACT (Advanced Clutch Technologys) 4 puck unsprung disc with their "Extreme" series pressure plate VERY positive engagment chips the tires into 4th at 110mph! (not really that hard when you have a clutch like this... i've driven basicly stock civics with the same clutch... they can do it too)We're about to but this same set up in BlackGTs car... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-03-2000||11:23 PM||||Yes but my car will still pull a friends 3.2 fastback before I had the nitrous! And my 1/4 times with out nitrous is a best of 14.7 and average of like 14.9-15.1. your right the 305 injectors will do just fine for your application, and up the pressure via an NOS pressure regulater (blocks the flow of fuel back to the tank {return line}increasing the pressure to whatever you need... or till the pump dies) Oh get an air/fuel meter both HAl-tec and autometer make nice pieces and thier VERY accurate. Available at Racer Wholesale (illinois) or summit catalog... (i'm sure there is a closer Autometer retailer to you... )<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||03-03-2000||11:34 PM||||ok...I'm a little confused about the "to 36#-55#(peak) stock cobra mustang (sn95)injectors" 1FST2M6 was saying.  First, stock cobra injectors on either the 5.0 or DOHC 4.6 were only bosch 24lb injectors (rated at 40 psi of pressure).  Your injector can act bigger under more pressure (there is a limit to it tho), but they were designed to run at a specific pressure (the 40 psi).   I'm running bosch 36lb injectors on my Stang (at 40psi), and jump the pressure to around 68lb of fuel pressure (which is actually only 55 psi of fuel pressure, because you have to subtract the amount of boost you are pushing through the manifold, where the injectors squirt the fuel, at 13lb of boost) at full boost.  This is supporting 500+ rwhp.  What fuel pressure are you running for those injectors?  What color are the injectors (brown top = 19lb, light blue top = 24lb, red top = 30lb, dark blue top = 36lb). <P>I blieve the stock injectors on the Fiero are Lucus, which are disc type.  If you want high pressure, then I'd suggest the pental type (bosch), because they can support higher pressures than the disc type.  I've heard (never seen it tho) that the disc type likes to close shut at over 60-70 psi.  I've never seen a pental type (and I've seen many go OVER 100 psi) do that.    <P>I just want to clear some air and ask some questions, not to flame.  Sorry for the book I just wrote....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||03-04-2000||12:15 AM||||Their Black And have a sticker that says RC on them (kinda like the RC cola label) I'm just reading what the print out says from RC. their located in Torrance, California uuum  here... <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rceng.com/</A>   I got  six different print outs of these on a flow bench all within 3% of each other. And the fuel pressure numbers are what the fuel pressure guage reads when its added inline to the NOS fuel pressure saftey switch at the schrader valve and taped to the rear window. Once again just what i'm reading... or have seen in the window, i wish i knew more.. sorry.. i'm not really up on everthing that makes it work just what i've changed and can read on the dyno print out or these flow charts. I'm not trying to lead anyone astray or what-have-you just reciting what i have and sharing personal experiance. I don't mean to sound defensive but i really don't know!  Thats why i have someone else to make it work... cause they have the clue the idea and the know how that I'm not equipped with. My cars fun to drive a blast to pick a fight with and expensive to insure. I can send a list of new goodies i've changed, had changed and their dyno results... but i can't tell ya why everything did what it did or why it's not worth a crap... just have a basic working knowledge of whats going on... and have always had the shop to point me in the next direction.. and since i've been pretty sucsessful following thier path i'll pass on the same directions... ||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||03-04-2000||01:12 AM||||as for my motor... Stock bottom end! 96,416 miles on it as of 20 minutes ago... heads are stock but the valves are from SI. (Fiero Store) and Fel-pro valve stem seals. Fel-pro head gaskets. Extrude honded upper and lower intake,Powder Coated them, Gasket matched them to the fel-pro gasket set i have, 2mm port, polish (re-butterfly) throttle body (Fiero Store offers a better one a 3mm piece) K&N breather element with tube and filter into sealed catch can. Blocked recirc/breather tube hole on intake boot. read about that at <A HREF="http://www.club4ag.com" TARGET=_blank>www.club4ag.com</A>  (sorry its a toyota web site) but it stops my intake from getting all oily and nasty, and restricting the air flow. Removed the resonator box and replaced it with 3" aluminum tube. an nicer version of this is available at... <A HREF="http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/" TARGET=_blank>http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/</A> ||||reg||1
